# Per-agent settings. Copy to ~/.bizzybot/settings.env and edit.
# Every key here is also passed to the `claude` subprocess as an env var.
# Real environment variables override anything set here.

# --- Model provider: OpenRouter (optional) ---
# Set BOTH to run this agent's Claude Code sessions against OpenRouter instead
# of Anthropic. Setting only one is ignored.
# See https://openrouter.ai/docs/cookbook/coding-agents/claude-code-integration
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5

# --- PR review poller (optional) ---
# These also work here, not just in the wrapper's .env — see .env.example for
# what they do. None of them is a secret, but note the caveat at the top of this
# file: every key here is exported into the `claude` subprocess.
# PR_REVIEW_CHANNEL=C0123456789
# PR_REVIEW_LOGIN=@me
# PR_POLL_INTERVAL_S=60

# --- Mailgun (optional) ---
# NOT needed for auto-replying to inbound email — that flow gets its key from
# Central per message and never exposes it to Claude (see docs/EMAIL.md). Set
# these ONLY if you want Claude itself to send arbitrary mail via Bash; they are
# passed to the claude subprocess as env vars (a standing capability).
# MAILGUN_API_KEY=key-...
# MAILGUN_DOMAIN=mail.yourco.com
# MAILGUN_BASE_URL=https://api.mailgun.net
